<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SDP RETAINS CLEAR LEAD IN JAN POLL - RADIO.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SDP RETAINS CLEAR LEAD IN JAN POLL - RADIO.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's biggest political</p>
<p>party, the Social Democrats, retained its clear lead in an</p>
<p>opinion poll in January, Finnish radio news reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The survey was made by polling institute Taloustutkimus Oy</p>
<p>between January 7 and February 5 among 1,919 people of voting</p>
<p>age. (Previous surveys also by Taloustutkimus, figs in pct):</p>
<p>			Jan    Dec    Nov   Election '96  Election '95</p>
<p> SDP		  24.8   25.3   25.5	24.5	    28.3</p>
<p> Conservatives    21.2   19.7   21.9	21.6	    17.9</p>
<p> Centre Party     20.2   20.0   22.8	21.8	    19.8</p>
<p> Green Party	 9.8   11.8    9.4	 6.3	     6.5</p>
<p> Leftist Alliance  9.1    7.7    8.8	10.4	    11.2</p>
<p> Swedish Party     4.7    5.1    4.7	 5.5	     5.1</p>
<p> Young Finns	 3.7    3.9    3.0	 1.3	     2.8</p>
<p> Christian League  3.3    3.0    2.5	 3.2	     3.0</p>
<p> Perussuomalaiset  1.0    1.0    0.7	 0.9	     1.3</p>
<p> Others		1.7    1.5    0.6	 4.1	     3.5</p>
<p>NOTE -- Election '96 is local government election held in</p>
<p>October last year and Election '95 is parliament election held</p>
<p>in March 1995. The next general election is due in March 1999.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
